  "title": "# Skins: finish and land (run 4) Read CLAUDE.md and the rules first.",
  "asked": "# Skins: finish and land (run 4) Read CLAUDE.md and the rules first. One agent, no sub-agents. This carries on the skins build. The full original brief is at /root/axf-builds/skins/.brief.md; read it, then read /root/axf-builds/skins-r3/skins-r3.log and skins-r2.log to see where the last runs stopped (both died on usage limits mid-work). You start on claude/skins-r3, which already has 3 commits: skin@1 + app-look@1 with the Windows skin; Settings > Appearance as the Theme manager, CLI, API and hub snapshot; the skin picker dialog with preview, apply and reset, the four apps re-baked, and check-skin in CI. It is 38 commits behind main. Do: 1. Merge origin/main into this branch first and resolve conflicts. 2. Finish whatever the original brief still needs (compare it against the commits). The last run was fixing win-close icons (`close` -> `x`) and fixtures in framework/spec/fixtures when it stopped; check that landed and works. 3. Run every gate: tests, console tsc, check-theme, check-controls, plugin-lifecycle, menu-reach, help-coverage --check, check-skin. All green, never skip. 4. UI Review shots of the skin picker and Appearance on phone and desktop (group 'skins - <date>'), non-blocking. 5. Open a PR, add it to the merge queue, auto-merge when green. Update THREADS, the orchestrator and the report at _claude/builds/reports/skins.md. End with a phone-readable summary: PR link, what's in it, anything left for Brett. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
